Z||000000||MotherGoose||05-09-2000||12:16 PM||||Does anyone know where to find the scoops that sit on the engine louvers and go up over the roof?<P>I have only seen them once||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-09-2000||02:35 PM||||If these are what your looking for I.R.M. use to sell them. I'm not sure who sells them now. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/twin_Indy_scoops_1_1.jpg"> <P>I prefer the Indy style scoop like this:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Droside1_3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image13_1.jpg"> <P>I think there is a thread on these in the tech area titled "notchback scoops" go back about 3-4 days to read it or do a search for it.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||MotherGoose||05-09-2000||02:57 PM||||Where did ya get the scoop?  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||05-09-2000||03:22 PM||||Nice photos, Orief.<P>Question:  Would having the vista vent open defeat the function of the scoop?  I mean, it seems like having the roof popped up would act like an air dam, thus pushing the airflow up and over the scoop instead of into it.<P>Just wondering ...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||05-09-2000||03:49 PM||||I got my Indy scoop from IRM. It was $200. I made it fully functional.<BR>As for with the sunroof open I set the height of the scoop so that the air passing over the sunroof still gets into the scoop.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sheight.jpg"> <P><BR>(Just got a digital camera for my B-day, Can ya tell?)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||MotherGoose||05-09-2000||04:04 PM||||I have never heard of them, do they have a web site?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||05-09-2000||04:14 PM||||IRM does not have a website. You can call and get a catalog or you can E-mail them.<P>IRM<BR>18100 Cashell Road<BR>Rockville, Maryland 20853<BR>1-800-367-8423 or 1-301-948-3301<BR>Fax: 1-301-774-6909<BR>E-mail: IRMFIERO@aol.com<P>They have other body parts including the IMSA GTU and GTO Fiero body kit for $3500.00<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gokart||05-09-2000||09:51 PM||||Had the ones in the first picture on my first Fiero 5 years ago. Got them from the Fiero Store but I don't think they have them anymore. Painted them black and they did look sharp...but the ol'tech issue of the Fieros air flow should be considered.<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||WisconsinGT||05-09-2000||11:41 PM||||Oreif, Can you take a few more picts of your scoop? I would like to see the scoop from different angles on your car. Is it difficult to look out the back window? How do you lift the back deck lid? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||05-10-2000||01:24 AM||||Here are some more pics. I tried to take a view out the back from the rear view mirror but it's hard to see. I'll have to do it on an outdoors shot. The view is only blocked in the middle. I have to take the scoop off to open the decklid. It uses 4 stainless steel hex bolts. Takes about 2 minutes to remove it. As soon as I find someone to bend an aluminum tube I plan on ducting the air into the engine.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Scoop_1.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
