Z||000011||Monkeyman||05-10-2000||12:20 PM||||Oh, TOM...||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||05-10-2000||02:33 PM||||FOCOA use to sell them also. I think they wanted $325 for it (if you were not a member) and they had it set up as a functional scoop with a screen. I went to their website and they don't list parts anymore. So If someone is a member could you check and see if they are still available from them? The IRM scoop was originally designed by Diversified Glass. They also designed the IMSA body. IRM bought all the molds when DG went out of business. So I don't would have one.<P>Here's a link that might have some. They don't list prices and they call it an SD4 scoop. <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||1
